**Evaluating the Redesign**

I'm currently focused on the initial redesign. I've taken a look at the landing page and now I'm thinking about the reference image. The dark theme is good. I need to make sure the header stays, with the "AI 导演" text at the top, and then include a focused message.


**Considering Layout Revisions**

I'm now fully immersed in the layout redesign, specifically focusing on the bottom input area. The reference image is very useful. It seems important to detach the input area visually, creating a floating effect with the chips and input box. I'm keen on integrating a "Settings" section for resolution/aspect ratio, and incorporating a microphone icon placeholder. Also, the chips need to be moved to the top of the input text field. I need to make sure the general feeling of the "composer" panel is maintained.


**Examining Input Integration**

I'm now zeroing in on the input mechanisms. The reference images offer distinct perspectives. My focus is on the bottom container, specifically. I see that the chips are best suited to live above the input field, to maintain the "composer" design. I've noted a send button alongside the input text area, as well as helper text. I will continue thinking about the microphone button, and its placement.


**Implementing the New Design**

I'm now fully immersed in the new input area design, focusing on the reference image's layout. The floating panel concept is crucial, with either a glassmorphism or dark background, and rounded corners. I'm prioritizing the placeholder text, the 9:16 and 480P buttons at the bottom-left, and the green arrow button to the bottom-right.


**Analyzing Visual Hierarchy**

I'm now analyzing the visual hierarchy of the input area again, and the reference images are key. I'm noting the absence of chips in the current bottom card design, in the "full screen" reference image. However, the previous iteration used them. Perhaps they're hidden, or to be placed above the main text area. The reference image with the black background gives a clue on the bottom card's design.


**Integrating New Elements**

I'm now integrating the additional elements into the input area design. I've noted the need for placeholder text and helper text below the input field. I am also planning to include "Settings" buttons for aspect ratio and resolution in the bottom-left corner of the card. Finally, I'll place the send button at the bottom-right. I'm still trying to figure out if the chips are going to be implemented as well.


**Defining Input Area Components**

I'm now fully immersed in the design, and focused on the components for the new input area. I will keep the chips above the card, similar to the previous design. The input container will be fixed at the bottom with padding, and the inner card will have a dark background with rounded corners. I am planning on a transparent, full-width textarea, placeholder and helper text, and a row for settings and the send button.


**Constructing the Interface**

I'm now fully immersed in the design, and focused on the interface. The background will be black/dark. The input card will be a dark gray. The send button will be a green circle with a black arrow. The settings buttons will be gray pills with icons. I'm prioritizing the placeholder text "描述你想要的视频画面~" and the helper text "生成视频时长大概1~2min". I'll be implementing the "Composer Card" layout. I will be modifying the `InputArea.tsx`, `ChatInterface.tsx` and `App.tsx` files. Specifically, the input area will be a fixed bottom container, z-index 20, with a scrollable row above the main card. The main card will have a dark background, padding, and a textarea for input with placeholder styling.


**Revising Color Palette**

I'm now refining the color palette for the interface. I've noted the muted lime/green and the dark settings buttons. I'll test `#84cc16` and `#22c55e` for the send button. I'm also planning to add helper text that disappears when typing, and a flex container for the bottom row with the settings buttons and the send button.


**Adjusting Page Content**

I'm now revising the page content, focusing on the initial layout. While the input area is the key, I'll also adjust the header in `App.tsx` for consistency. The `InputArea.tsx` redesign remains my priority, specifically the Composer Card layout. I'm focusing on positioning chips above the card, and ensuring the card contains the input, helper text, settings, and send button, and that input text area can grow, or have a fixed height. I'll need to check the header in `App.tsx` and see how it might be updated to match the reference.


**Coding Input Area Logic**

I'm now fully immersed in coding the input area logic. I've noted the `inputValue`, `aspectRatio`, `resolution`, and `handleSend` states. I'm leaning toward maintaining 1080P/4K as the default resolution, as it is sensible, but will likely add an option to select 480P for a draft mode as I am following the reference image. I'll stick to the existing logic, just styling the implementation.


**Styling the Card Elements**

I'm now styling the card elements. I've focused on the text area, helper text, and the bottom row. I plan to use the `!inputValue` condition to display the helper text. I'm keen on the appearance and the behavior of the text area. The font sizing, placeholder color and helper text are essential. I'm prioritizing placeholder styling and helper text placement. I will add a flex container for the bottom row, with settings and the send button.


**Modifying App Header**

I'm now revising the application header. I've noted the need to align the `App.tsx` header with the reference image. The current implementation uses a centered title, which I will replace with a left arrow and a right bulb icon, respectively. I also confirmed that `types.ts` and `constants.ts` require no changes. The prompt is: "描述你想要的视频画面~" and helper "生成视频时长大概1~2min". I've already tested the color: `#84cc16`.


**Updating Visuals and Content**

I'm now integrating the updated placeholder text "描述你想要的视频画面~" and also adding the helper text "生成视频时长大概1~2min". I've selected `ArrowUp` from lucide-react for the send button. I'm carefully considering the "480P" button's styling and logic. I will also make sure to keep the chat interface. I'm focusing on the integration of these elements to align with the reference images.


**Implementing the "Card" Layout**

I'm now fully immersed in implementing the "Card" layout in `InputArea.tsx`. I'll remove the old "Bar" layout and update icons, colors, to match the reference, including darker grays and the green send button. I'll position the chips above the card and verify the padding and layout in `App.tsx`. I will adjust the background to `bg-black` or `bg-[#09090b]` to align with the reference images. I'm ready to proceed with generating the XML.

